  "summary": "Malicious code in testingnewflow (npm)",
  "details": "Testingnewflow@1.0.0 is a stub package (70 bytes, no real code) that declares a dependency safe-buffer-helper pinned to a non-registry URL (hxxps://artifacts[.]stg[.]yosiroute[.]com/npm/safe-buffer-helper). When installed, npm fetches this dependency from the attacker-controlled host, giving the attacker arbitrary code execution on the installer's machine. The package has no repository, no README content of substance, and no legitimate functionality — it exists solely as a dependency-confusion vector to pull remote code.",
